---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const toc = [
	{ id: 'information-we-collect', label: 'Information We Collect' },
	{ id: 'how-we-use-your-information', label: 'How We Use Your Information' },
	{ id: 'third-party-services', label: 'Third-Party Services' },
	{ id: 'data-retention-and-deletion', label: 'Data Retention and Deletion' },
	{ id: 'childrens-privacy', label: "Children's Privacy" },
	{ id: 'security', label: 'Security' },
	{ id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your Rights' },
	{ id: 'gdpr', label: 'European Union Users (GDPR)' },
	{ id: 'ccpa', label: 'California Residents (CCPA)' },
	{ id: 'uk-gdpr', label: 'UK Users (UK GDPR)' },
	{ id: 'australia-new-zealand', label: 'Australia and New Zealand' },
	{ id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to This Privacy Policy' },
	{ id: 'contact', label: 'Contact Us' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — Daisy's Dailies"
	description="How Daisy's Dailies collects, uses, and protects your data."
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	toc={toc}
>
	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> February 10, 2026</p>
	<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> November 13, 2026</p>

	<p>
		Welcome to Daisy's Dailies. Your privacy is critically important to us. This
		Privacy Policy explains how Sibert Strategy Group ("we," "us," or "our")
		collects, uses, and shares information through the Daisy's Dailies mobile
		application.
	</p>

	<h2 id="information-we-collect">1. Information We Collect</h2>

	<h3>A. Information You Provide to Us</h3>

	<Callout tone="info">
		<p>
			<strong>Account Data:</strong> When you create an account, we collect your email
			address and display name. If you sign up with Apple or Google, we receive your
			name and email from that provider.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>User Content:</strong> We store the task and errand data you input into
			the app, including flowers, petals, items, appointments, and address book
			entries.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Address Book:</strong> Address book entries are places you add yourself
			(name, address, notes). The app does not read your device's contacts.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Calendar Data:</strong> If you import calendar events, we read your device
			calendar to show you its events, and copy only the events you select. If you turn
			on Calendar Sync (Pro), events from the calendars you choose in Settings are copied
			automatically when you open the app, and updated when they change. For each event
			we copy its title, time, duration, and location. We never copy event notes. We do
			not store or transmit calendar data from calendars or events you have not chosen.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Support Emails:</strong> When you email us (Settings → Contact Us opens
			your email app), we receive your email address and whatever you write. We use it
			only to answer you.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>
			<strong>Voice Input (Microphone):</strong> If you hold the microphone button in Quick
			Add or in the AI route instructions, the app uses your phone's built-in speech
			recognition to turn what you say into text. Recognition runs entirely on your device:
			your voice is never recorded, stored, or sent to us or to any third party. Only the
			resulting text, which you can edit before sending, is used, exactly like text you type.
			The app asks for microphone and speech recognition permission the first time you press
			the button, and the button only appears where your phone can recognize speech offline.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h3>B. Automatically Collected Information</h3>

	<p>To ensure app stability and manage subscriptions, we automatically collect:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Device Identifiers:</strong> Firebase user ID and RevenueCat customer ID,
			linked to your account for authentication and subscription management.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP addresses, operating system versions, device model,
			and app crash logs (via Sentry).
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Crash &amp; Performance Data:</strong> Crash reports, stack traces, and performance
			metrics are collected by Sentry in production builds. Session replays may be captured
			to help diagnose errors. Your user ID, email and display name are attached to crash
			reports for attribution.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Push Notification Tokens:</strong> If you enable push notifications, we store
			your device's push token to deliver the notifications you have turned on, such as
			assignment alerts, reminders, and daily and weekly summaries. Tokens are automatically
			removed if unused for 30 days.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Usage Counts:</strong> We store with your account how many times you have opened
			the app and on how many days, to understand how the app is used.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Anonymous Usage Analytics:</strong> We use Aptabase, a privacy-focused analytics
			service, to count app events (for example, that a flower was created or a screen was
			opened) so we can see which features help. Each event carries the app version, operating
			system, app language, and a random session ID that resets after an hour of inactivity.
			Events never include your name, email, user ID, family ID, or anything you type. Aptabase
			uses your IP address only in memory to determine your country and region, and does not
			store it.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>C. Location Information</h3>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>
			Daisy's Dailies requests access to your device's Fine (exact) and Coarse (approximate)
			location.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Purpose:</strong> We use this data strictly to help you search for nearby places,
			bias search results to your current area for convenience, and display your location on
			a map when planning routes.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Usage:</strong> Location data is only accessed while you are actively using the
			location-based features of the app. We do not track your location in the background,
			nor do we use your location for advertising purposes.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="how-we-use-your-information">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>

	<p>We use the collected data to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Daisy's Dailies service.</li>
		<li>Authenticate your identity and manage your account.</li>
		<li>Process subscriptions and in-app purchases via RevenueCat.</li>
		<li>Monitor and analyze app performance and stability (via Sentry).</li>
		<li>Deliver the push notifications you have turned on.</li>
		<li>Import the calendar events you select, and keep the calendars you choose in sync (Pro).</li>
		<li>Understand which features are used, through anonymous usage analytics.</li>
		<li>Answer your emails and troubleshoot technical issues.</li>
		<li>
			Provide AI features (AI route optimization, Quick Add, and Plan My Week) using Google
			Gemini, only when you start them. See Section 3 for exactly what is sent.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="third-party-services">3. Third-Party Services</h2>

	<p>We use trusted third-party service providers to help run the app. These include:</p>

	<Callout tone="info">
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Google Firebase:</strong> For authentication, database hosting (Firestore), and cloud functions.</li>
			<li><strong>Sentry:</strong> For crash reporting, error tracking, performance monitoring, and session replays.</li>
			<li><strong>Google Maps &amp; Places API:</strong> To provide mapping and location search functionality.</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Google Gemini:</strong> For the app's AI features. Nothing is sent unless you
				start one of them. Free accounts get a limited number of AI requests; Pro includes a
				monthly allowance.
				<ul>
					<li><em>AI route optimization:</em> the names, addresses, coordinates, durations, scheduled times, and priorities of the stops in your route, plus any extra instructions you add.</li>
					<li><em>Quick Add:</em> the text you type or say, the names of your flowers, your app language, time zone, and today's date. Family members' first names are replaced with placeholders before anything is sent.</li>
					<li><em>Plan My Week (Pro):</em> the names, times, and durations of the stops being planned, their locations rounded to about 1 km, your available hours, your app language, and time zone.</li>
				</ul>
				No account identifiers or family member names are sent to Gemini.
			</li>
			<li><strong>RevenueCat:</strong> To manage in-app subscriptions and purchase validation.</li>
			<li><strong>Expo:</strong> For push notification delivery.</li>
			<li><strong>Aptabase:</strong> For anonymous usage analytics, as described in Section 1B.</li>
		</ul>
	</Callout>

	<p>These services may collect and process data according to their own privacy policies:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RevenueCat Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sentry Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://expo.dev/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Expo Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://aptabase.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aptabase Privacy Policy</a></li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="data-retention-and-deletion">4. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>

	<p>
		We retain your information for as long as your account is active. You can delete any
		flower, petal, appointment, or address book entry at any time, which removes it from our
		servers.
	</p>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>
			<strong>Automatic Data Cleanup:</strong> Appointments are automatically deleted 30 days
			after their scheduled date. Push notification tokens are automatically removed if unused
			for 30 days.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>
			<strong>Account Deletion:</strong> You have the right to delete your account and all associated
			personal data at any time through the Settings menu within the app. Upon account deletion,
			your data will be removed from our active databases immediately and permanently deleted
			from our servers within 30 days.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<p>
		For detailed instructions on how to delete your data, please visit our
		<a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion Instructions</a> page.
	</p>

	<h2 id="childrens-privacy">5. Children's Privacy</h2>

	<p>
		Daisy's Dailies is intended for users who are 13 years of age or older. We require all users
		to confirm they meet this age requirement before creating an account. We do not knowingly
		collect personal information from children under 13.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Family Members:</strong> The app includes a family sharing feature. All family members
		who access the app must create their own account and independently confirm they are 13 or older.
		Children are not added to families without their own account — they join by accepting an invite,
		which requires completing the age-confirmed signup flow.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>EU Users:</strong> If you are located in the European Union, you must be at least 16
		years of age to create an account, in accordance with GDPR Article 8. Some EU member states
		permit a lower age of 13 with parental consent; however, we apply the 16-year threshold uniformly
		across all EU countries for simplicity.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>If we discover a violation:</strong> If we become aware that a user under the applicable
		minimum age has created an account, we will promptly delete that account and all associated
		personal data. Parents or guardians who believe their child has registered may contact us at
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
		to request immediate account deletion.
	</p>

	<h2 id="security">6. Security</h2>

	<p>
		We implement industry-standard security measures (such as Firebase's secure authentication
		and encrypted data transit) to protect your information. However, no method of electronic
		transmission is 100% secure.
	</p>

	<h2 id="your-rights">7. Your Rights</h2>

	<p>Depending on your location, you may have certain rights regarding your personal information, including:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The right to access your personal data</li>
		<li>The right to correct inaccurate data</li>
		<li>The right to delete your data</li>
		<li>The right to withdraw consent</li>
		<li>The right to data portability</li>
	</ul>

	<p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the information below.</p>

	<h2 id="gdpr">8. European Union Users (GDPR)</h2>

	<p>
		If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), your personal information is processed
		in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). This section explains our
		lawful basis for processing and your enhanced rights.
	</p>

	<h3>A. Lawful Basis for Processing</h3>

	<p>
		We process your personal data only where we have a lawful basis to do so. The table below sets
		out the legal basis for each category of processing:
	</p>

	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Data / Processing Activity</th>
				<th>Lawful Basis</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Account registration (email, display name)</td>
				<td><strong>Contract</strong> — necessary to provide the service</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>User content (flowers, petals, items, appointments, address book entries)</td>
				<td><strong>Contract</strong> — core function of the service</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Device identifiers, technical data, crash logs</td>
				<td><strong>Legitimate Interests</strong> — maintaining app stability and security</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Support emails</td>
				<td><strong>Legitimate Interests</strong> — responding to user enquiries</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Usage counts and anonymous usage analytics</td>
				<td><strong>Legitimate Interests</strong> — understanding which features are used so we can improve the app</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Location data</td>
				<td><strong>Consent</strong> — requested via device permission prompt</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Push notification tokens</td>
				<td><strong>Consent</strong> — requested via device permission prompt</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Calendar data</td>
				<td><strong>Consent</strong> — you choose which events to import or which calendars to sync</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Sentry session replays</td>
				<td><strong>Consent</strong> — opt-in toggle in Settings → Privacy</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>AI features: route optimization, Quick Add, Plan My Week (Google Gemini)</td>
				<td><strong>Consent</strong> — you start each request yourself</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h3>B. Your GDPR Rights</h3>

	<p>Under GDPR, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Right of Access (Art. 15):</strong> Request a copy of all personal data we hold about you, including via the data export feature in Settings.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Rectification (Art. 16):</strong> Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Erasure (Art. 17):</strong> Request deletion of your data. You can do this at any time via Settings → Delete Account, or by contacting us.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Restriction (Art. 18):</strong> Request that we restrict processing of your data while a dispute is resolved.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Data Portability (Art. 20):</strong> Receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format via the export feature in Settings.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Object (Art. 21):</strong> Object to processing based on legitimate interests. We will cease unless we can demonstrate compelling grounds.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time (e.g., revoke location or microphone permission in your device settings, turn off Calendar Sync or session replay in Settings).</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>C. International Data Transfers</h3>

	<p>
		Our service providers (Firebase, Sentry, RevenueCat, Expo, Google Gemini) are based in the
		United States. Transfers of personal data from the EEA to these providers are covered by Standard
		Contractual Clauses (SCCs) as provided by each processor's Data Processing Agreement.
	</p>

	<h3>D. Right to Complain</h3>

	<p>
		You have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority.
		A list of EU data protection authorities is available at
		<a href="https://edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/about-edpb/members_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">edpb.europa.eu</a>.
	</p>

	<h3>E. Data Retention (GDPR)</h3>

	<p>We retain your data only as long as necessary for the purpose it was collected:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Account data:</strong> Retained until account deletion</li>
		<li><strong>User content (flowers, petals, items):</strong> Retained until deleted by you or account deletion</li>
		<li><strong>Address book entries:</strong> Retained until deleted by you or account deletion</li>
		<li><strong>Appointments:</strong> Auto-deleted 30 days after scheduled date</li>
		<li><strong>Push notification tokens:</strong> Auto-deleted after 30 days of inactivity</li>
		<li><strong>Support emails:</strong> Retained up to 2 years for customer service purposes</li>
		<li><strong>Anonymous usage analytics (Aptabase):</strong> Retained up to 5 years; these events cannot be linked to you</li>
		<li><strong>Transaction records:</strong> Retained as required by law (typically 7 years)</li>
		<li><strong>Crash logs (Sentry):</strong> Retained per Sentry's 90-day default retention</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="ccpa">9. California Residents (CCPA)</h2>

	<p>
		If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) grants you the
		following rights regarding your personal information:
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> You have the right to request disclosure of the categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you, the sources from which we collected it, the business purpose for collecting it, and the categories of third parties with whom we share it.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> You have the right to request deletion of personal information we have collected from you, subject to certain exceptions.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Opt-Out of Sale:</strong> You have the right to opt out of the sale of your personal information. See our statement below.</li>
		<li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> You have the right not to receive discriminatory treatment for exercising any of your CCPA rights.</li>
	</ul>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>
			<strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> Daisy's Dailies does not sell, rent,
			or trade your personal information to third parties for monetary or other valuable consideration.
			We share data only with the service providers listed in Section 3 of this policy, solely for
			the purpose of operating the app on your behalf.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<p>
		To exercise your rights under the CCPA, please contact us at
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
		with the subject line "California Privacy Request." We will respond within 45 days of receiving
		your request.
	</p>

	<h2 id="uk-gdpr">10. UK Users (UK GDPR)</h2>

	<p>
		If you are located in the United Kingdom, your personal information is processed in accordance
		with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.
	</p>

	<p>
		You have the same rights as EU users described in Section 8 of this policy, enforceable under
		UK law. These include the right to access, correct, delete, restrict processing, port your data,
		and object to processing.
	</p>

	<p>
		To lodge a complaint about our data practices, you may contact the UK Information Commissioner's
		Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		For any UK-specific data enquiries, please contact us at
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="australia-new-zealand">11. Australia and New Zealand</h2>

	<h3>Australia — Australian Privacy Act 1988</h3>

	<p>
		Daisy's Dailies complies with the Australian Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy
		Principles (APPs). This policy constitutes our APP Privacy Policy as required under APP 1.
	</p>

	<p>
		You have the right to access the personal information we hold about you and to request corrections
		if that information is inaccurate, out of date, incomplete, or misleading. To make such a request,
		please contact us at
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
	</p>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>
			<strong>Notifiable Data Breaches:</strong> In the event of an eligible data breach that is likely
			to result in serious harm to any affected individuals, we will notify the Office of the Australian
			Information Commissioner (OAIC) and all affected users within 30 days of becoming aware of the
			breach. Notifications will describe the nature of the breach, the information involved, and the
			steps we are taking in response.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h3>New Zealand — Privacy Act 2020</h3>

	<p>
		Daisy's Dailies complies with the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020 and its Information Privacy Principles
		(IPPs). In the event of a notifiable privacy breach that poses a risk of serious harm, we will notify
		the New Zealand Privacy Commissioner and affected individuals as soon as practicable. New Zealand
		users may direct privacy complaints or access requests to us at
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
		or to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner at
		<a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy.org.nz</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="changes">12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

	<p>
		We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make changes, we will update the
		"Last Updated" date at the top of this policy. We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy
		periodically to stay informed about how we are protecting your information.
	</p>

	<h2 id="contact">13. Contact Us</h2>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us at:</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Sibert Strategy Group</strong><br />
			Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<hr />

	<p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
		For information on how to delete your data, please see our
		<a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion Instructions</a>.
		See also our <a href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
